ent": " Working with Variables", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Take Away", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!"}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.", "type": "text"}]}]}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}]}], "type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Variables in Javascript", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 3, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 3, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you hear or use to talk about JavaScript.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Understand information about web applications, their principles and basic concepts in a range of work contexts.   Describe applications for an operating system for personal computers in a range of work contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.  Exchanges simple information on web applications, and applications for operating systems for personal computers.", "type": "secondary_1"}]}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob03re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Conditional Sentences With If Clauses- Question Form", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "A<b> conditional sentence</b> states something that happens, will happen, could have happened or could happen depending on a condition.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<b>Conditional clauses</b> are called like this because they talk about situations that need a condition to be true or not. There are different types of <b>conditional sentences</b> that express how likely is for something to take place or how probable was it for a given situation to take place in the past or as a result of an unreal event.<br/><br/>  The usual <b>conditional sentence</b> is composed of two clauses: the \u201c<strong>if clause</strong>\u201d that explains the condition, and the \u2018<strong>main clause</strong>' that presents the result or consequence.<br/><br/>  When asking questions with <b>conditional sentences</b>, you can put the \u201c<strong>if clause</strong>\u201d or the \u201c<strong>result clause</strong>\u201d at the beginning, just bear in mind that when you put the \u201c<strong>if clause</strong>\u201d at the end, you don't need to use a comma.<br/><br/>   Examples:<br/> <span class=\"italic\"><b>Would I have passed</b> the exam <b>if I had studied </b>the primitive data types?<br/><b> If we don't write </b>these variables correctly, <b>will it be too hard</b> to fix the code in the future?</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If you have spare time, will you explain to me something about data types in JavaScript?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Will you correct me if I'm mistaken? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If JavaScript is untyped language, does it mean that it isn't necessary to specify the value of data types from the beginning?", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Passive Voice of Modal Verbs, Should, in Negative Form", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "The <strong>passive</strong> voice focuses on the thing or person that receives the action rather than on the agent that performs it. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The <b>passive voice</b> highlights the thing or person that receives an action. When we use <strong>passive voice</strong>, we could indicate who the agent that carries out the action is, or we could omit it if the context allows it.<br/><br/>  Whenever we are using <strong>passive voice</strong>, we can introduce <strong>modal verbs</strong> to specify if the action expresses probability, necessity or obligation, among others.<br/><br/>  Let's check the following example:<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">Symbols in JavaScript <b>shouldn't be miswritten</b>.</span><br/><br/>  The emphasis in this sentence is placed on \u201csymbols in JavaScript\u201d and what not to do with them, instead of whoever miswrote the symbols.<br/><br/>  The <b>passive voice</b> with modal verbs in negative form follows this structure:<br/><br/>  <div class=\"center_text\">Thing or person that receives the action + <b>modal in negative</b>+ <b>be</b> + <b>past participle</b></div><br/><br/>  Examples:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">JavaScript <strong>mustn't be regarded</strong> as a difficult programming language to use.<br/>  All these variables <strong>couldn't have been named</strong> by my brother last night.</span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The process of storing a value in a variable is called variable initialization which shouldn't be restricted only to the moment in which a variable is created. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You shouldn't need to indicate the type of value that the variable will be holding during the variable declaration. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You mustn't be interrupted while grading those exams.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "JavaScript Reserved Words", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "There is a list of words that cannot be used for variables or other objects as they can create confusion within the JavaScript system. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Here is a list of the words that shouldn't be used as object names in JavaScript.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":14,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"abstract\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"boolean\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"break\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"byte\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"case\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"catch\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"char\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"class\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"const\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"continue\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"debugger\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"default\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"delete\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"do\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"double\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"else\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"enum\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"export\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"extends\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"false\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"final\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"finally\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"float\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"for\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"function\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"goto\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"if\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"implements\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":8,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"import\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"in\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"instanceof\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"int\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"interface\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"long\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"native\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"new\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"null\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"package\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"private\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"protected\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"public\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"return\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"short\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"static\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"super\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"switch\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"synchronized\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"this\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"throw\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"transient\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"true\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"try\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"typeof\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"var\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"void\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"volatile\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"while\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"with\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "spare ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "when you have extra quantity of something  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If you have spare time, will you explain to me something about data types in JavaScript?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob03aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "Boolean", "type": "name"}, {"content": "algebraic concept in which there are only two possible values: true or false  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: JavaScript accepts three types of primitive data: numbers, strings of text and Boolean which has only two states: true and false. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob03aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "placed", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be located or organized  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Ok, data can be placed in groups which are named with the keyword \"var\". Those groups are what we call variables. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob03aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "have to do with something", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be linked to something or be related to a subject  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It has to do with the region of the program in which it is defined.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob03aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "scope ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the reach or extent of something  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: JavaScript has only two scopes: global variables which can be defined at anyplace in the JavaScript code; and local variables which will be visible only within the function where they are defined.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob03aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "untyped language ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a language that does not need to have a type declaration", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If JavaScript is untyped language, does it mean that it isn't necessary to specify the value of data types from the beginning?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob03aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Search for more information about data types in JavaScript.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Create a chart with the different data types where you include a definition and examples.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Choose one data type and prepare a poster.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your poster with the class. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I understand what the primitive data types in JavaScript are.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I identify variables in JavaScript.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I know the difference between global and local variables. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my work with the classmates.", "type": "text"}]}]}